name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q12_2025'

question 'When evaluating a filter\'s inclusivity, a developer should look for:'

wrong 'Whether the filter makes the app run faster.'
wrong 'If the filter labels are written in all capital letters.'
right 'Whether the filter categories or thresholds accidentally exclude or sideline certain groups of people.'
wrong 'If the AI can guess what the user wants to filter before they type it.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 9

Inclusive design involves analyzing if your algorithmic choices (like filtering for only "Standard" families) unintentionally marginalize or ignore specific stakeholders.
MARKDOWN
